# gap[077] proof: MULTIPLE ASSIGNMENT IS SIMULTANEOUS.
#
# `a, b = b, a` is the swap every reader already has a reflex for, and it was
# SILENTLY WRONG. The targets were written left to right, so `a` took `b`'s
# value and then `b` took the ALREADY-OVERWRITTEN `a`. Measured 2026-08-09
# before the repair: `a = 1 · b = 2 · a, b = b, a` printed `2 2`, and
# `t[1], t[2] = t[2], t[1]` over `{ 3, 7 }` printed `7 7`. BOTH BACKENDS
# AGREED on both wrong answers, which is exactly why it read as the language
# rather than as a defect — a differential could not convict it.
#
# Verified BY VALUE, never by exit status: a two-element swap that half worked
# is easy to misread through an 8-bit status, and `{7,7}` looks like a swap
# that half succeeded rather than like a language defect.
#
# FOUR ROWS, and the last two are the controls:
#   swap through a table            the original repro
#   swap through plain locals       the same defect without indexing
#   computed indices                `i` and `j` read once each, not twice
#   NEGATIVE TWIN — no overlap      `p, q = 8, 9` must keep its shape; the
#                                   repair fires only on a real conflict
#   POSITIVE CONTROL — the pack     `v, w = two(4)` is ONE value adjusted to
#                                   two positions. It already worked, it must
#                                   not regress, and if it ever reaches the
#                                   simultaneous path it will still read 8/12
#                                   — so it is also the shape check.
#   SIDE-EFFECTING INDICES          a key expression must be evaluated ONCE;
#                                   `calls` is 2, and a naive temp rewrite
#                                   that re-runs the index reads 4.

calls = 0

bump(k: i64): i64
  calls = calls + 1
  k

two(x: i64): any
  return x * 2, x * 3

want(what: str, got: i64, wanted: i64): i64
  if got != wanted
    print("simultaneous assign: {what} got {got}, want {wanted}")
    os.exit(1)
  0

main(): i64
  t = { 3, 7 }
  t[1], t[2] = t[2], t[1]
  want("table swap first", t[1], 7)
  want("table swap second", t[2], 3)

  a = 1
  b = 2
  a, b = b, a
  want("local swap first", a, 2)
  want("local swap second", b, 1)

  i = 1
  j = 2
  t[i], t[j] = t[j], t[i]
  want("computed index swap first", t[1], 3)
  want("computed index swap second", t[2], 7)

  p = 5
  q = 6
  p, q = 8, 9
  want("negative twin first", p, 8)
  want("negative twin second", q, 9)

  v, w = two(4)
  want("pack first", v, 8)
  want("pack second", w, 12)

  u = { 3, 7 }
  u[bump(1)], u[bump(2)] = u[2], u[1]
  want("effect index swap first", u[1], 7)
  want("effect index swap second", u[2], 3)
  want("effect index evaluated once each", calls, 2)

  print("simultaneous assign: OK")
  0
